From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: descriptor DMA for the gadget on Sophgo CV18XX/SG200X

The upstream parameters for sophgo,cv1800b-usb disable DMA, so the gadget
runs in slave mode: the CPU moves every packet through the FIFOs in the
interrupt handler. With HID and UAC1 audio that is 5,000-10,000 interrupts
per second, 5-10 % of the C906. The SoC vendor kernel (cv182x params)
enables g_dma and g_dma_desc for the same controller, and GHWCFG2/4 report
internal and descriptor DMA. Host mode keeps host_dma off.

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
index 091bfcfef..a95a53384 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -225,7 +225,14 @@ static void dwc2_set_cv1800_params(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	p->otg_caps.hnp_support = false;
 	p->otg_caps.srp_support = false;
 	p->host_dma = false;
-	p->g_dma = false;
+	/*
+	 * Gadget transfers by descriptor DMA, as in the SoC vendor kernel
+	 * (cv182x params: g_dma, g_dma_desc). In slave mode the CPU moves every
+	 * packet through the FIFOs in the interrupt handler: with HID and UAC1
+	 * audio that was 5,000-10,000 interrupts per second on the C906.
+	 */
+	p->g_dma = true;
+	p->g_dma_desc = true;
 	p->speed = DWC2_SPEED_PARAM_HIGH;
 	p->phy_type = DWC2_PHY_TYPE_PARAM_UTMI;
 	p->phy_utmi_width = 16;
